1
00:02:03,755 --> 00:02:07,965
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:10,297 --> 00:02:41,397
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:47,150
What’s your final decision, brother?

4
00:02:49,325 --> 00:02:50,950
Did you come to a conclusion?

5
00:02:52,725 --> 00:02:55,335
You disobeyed the orders once again,
Osman Bey.

6
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,075
You will get arrested.

7
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,925
Who is going to do that, brother?

8
00:03:02,575 --> 00:03:03,475
Alps!

9
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:05,450
Arrest him!

10
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:07,250
In the name of Allah!

11
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,375
Don’t you dare!

12
00:03:14,975 --> 00:03:16,525
Don’t you dare!

13
00:03:16,950 --> 00:03:18,400
I’m talking to you Alps!

14
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:27,350
Sheathe your swords!

15
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:31,600
May you not stir up trouble, Bamsı Bey!

16
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,975
I’m the Head Alp here!

17
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:40,875
Savcı Bey, the Head Alp.

18
00:03:43,975 --> 00:03:45,400
Oh folks!

19
00:03:48,075 --> 00:03:49,400
Oh folks!

20
00:03:51,375 --> 00:03:52,625
Listen to me!

21
00:03:53,875 --> 00:03:56,800
If you want to see a Head Alp…

22
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,925
… look right here!

23
00:04:02,675 --> 00:04:07,775
However, if you want to see the Kayı Bey…

24
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:12,550
… look right there!

25
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:17,875
He is the one who took your prisoner
brothers back...

26
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:23,800
... while you were busy talking here!

27
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:33,475
Who can say a word to him now?

28
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,125
I can!

29
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:45,500
You huh?

30
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,425
Yes, me!

31
00:04:48,550 --> 00:04:49,725
Enough!

32
00:04:58,625 --> 00:05:00,375
Enough already!

33
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,325
I’m your big brother!

34
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:16,650
Osman, you will not stand against the
Head Alp!

35
00:05:20,575 --> 00:05:27,100
And Savcı, you will not will arrest your
brother because of this reason!

36
00:05:31,075 --> 00:05:32,250
Brother!

37
00:05:33,575 --> 00:05:36,325
You were giving me lectures about being
a brother!

38
00:05:36,650 --> 00:05:38,300
Take your hands off my brother!

39
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,450
Savcı Bey, hurry up!

40
00:06:06,875 --> 00:06:08,250
Our Bey is dying!

41
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:11,650
Our father is dying!

42
00:06:25,975 --> 00:06:26,825
Father.

43
00:06:57,875 --> 00:07:01,875
Whatever happens, they are brothers.

44
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:07,400
They are the sons of Ertuğrul Gazi.

45
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:30,975
There are news from our spies in Black
Sea region.

46
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,975
Supporting forces are coming to
Kulacahisar.

47
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:38,000
Ertuğrul is on his death bed and his sons
are fighting for Beyhood.

48
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,325
With this news, he may pretty well be
dead by now.

49
00:07:43,675 --> 00:07:46,975
Soon, you will get the revenge of your
father from the Turks.

50
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,220
After you hear your new duty, you will
thank me since I dissuaded you from death.

51
00:07:51,225 --> 00:07:53,650
Just like Caesar during the battle of
Axona...

52
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:55,875
… you will kill every Turk you see.

53
00:07:58,850 --> 00:08:00,600
With pleasure, Nikola.

54
00:08:00,650 --> 00:08:03,975
Thinking that we would attack, they
increased their defence.

55
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,075
But Osman saw what I am able to do.

56
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,300
With the forces coming to Kulacahisar…

57
00:08:10,925 --> 00:08:13,950
… we will bite them like a snake at an
unexpected time.

58
00:08:22,675 --> 00:08:24,520
2 DAYS LATER

59
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:26,900
Don’t be hard on yourself.

60
00:08:28,025 --> 00:08:31,600
Who knows, maybe he will stand up like
nothing has happened.

61
00:08:33,125 --> 00:08:34,500
Isn’t it possible, Osman?

62
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,799
He is sleeping all day.

63
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:43,125
I’ve never seen my father like that
before.

64
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,550
All he is doing is puking blood.

65
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,700
Osman.

66
00:08:56,725 --> 00:08:58,150
What about my brother?

67
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,250
He was going to arrest me.

68
00:09:01,425 --> 00:09:03,300
You listen to nobody's words, Osman.

69
00:09:04,625 --> 00:09:05,800
You always do you.

70
00:09:06,275 --> 00:09:08,725
Everything happens because of this reason.

71
00:09:11,025 --> 00:09:12,375
You are too aggressive.

72
00:09:12,775 --> 00:09:15,575
When you are angry, you become unbearable.

73
00:09:18,170 --> 00:09:20,400
-You are too aggressive and…
-My Bala.

74
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,300
Have I sickened you?

75
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:29,250
You are never free from troubles, my
Osman.

76
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:32,000
Please continue.

77
00:09:32,975 --> 00:09:35,000
Are there more things you want to say?

78
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:36,775
Indeed there are.

79
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:40,325
I’m also dragged after those troubles.

80
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:44,775
Have I really tortured you this much?

81
00:09:44,825 --> 00:09:50,225
Of course not, the real torture starts if
I’m not dragged after those very troubles.

82
00:09:53,125 --> 00:09:55,675
I can give my life for the troubles
you bring.

83
00:10:03,075 --> 00:10:04,250
My Bala…

84
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:16,425
… my Savcı brother is being provoked by
Yalvak.

85
00:10:17,475 --> 00:10:19,950
He is using my brother and uncle against
me.

86
00:10:20,025 --> 00:10:21,725
You should talk to your brother.

87
00:10:21,725 --> 00:10:25,525
I can try but he has become blind as to
his ambitions.

88
00:10:27,725 --> 00:10:29,825
However, it can’t continue like this.

89
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:36,525
Will he listen to me if I suggest
him to go to Kulacahisar together?

90
00:10:36,925 --> 00:10:39,225
He will say we should wait to get
stronger.

91
00:10:41,025 --> 00:10:43,875
However, those mischiefs, Nikola and
Flatyos...

92
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:45,800
… are they going to wait?

93
00:10:48,025 --> 00:10:49,375
No, they are not going to.

94
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,100
And I’m not going to wait either.

95
00:10:52,750 --> 00:10:54,325
I’m going to kill both of them!

96
00:10:56,625 --> 00:10:59,650
I will enter that castle and cut their
their throats!

97
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,955
How are you going to enter that castle?

98
00:11:01,955 --> 00:11:02,985
I’ll manage, my Bala!

99
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,950
Among all those soldiers, how are you
going to manage that?

100
00:11:07,350 --> 00:11:10,425
Please hold your horses, Osman.

101
00:11:12,050 --> 00:11:14,425
It’s not the time to wait, my Bala.

102
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:18,400
Since the fall of Kulacahisar, the time
has been ticking against us.

103
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:21,685
They will become stronger once
they get support from Constantinople.

104
00:11:21,695 --> 00:11:24,170
When that happens, how are we going to
find support?

105
00:11:49,975 --> 00:11:52,900
My Bey, Zulfikar brother brought
important news.

106
00:11:53,125 --> 00:11:54,250
Tell me, Zulfikar!

107
00:11:54,275 --> 00:11:57,375
Osman Bey, the supporting forces have
arrived at Kulacahisar.

108
00:12:04,075 --> 00:12:06,170
Who are they and how many of them there
are?

109
00:12:06,425 --> 00:12:09,125
I don’t know their numbers but they are
all cavaliers.

110
00:12:09,750 --> 00:12:10,775
Kuman cavaliers.

111
00:12:11,125 --> 00:12:12,200
Kuman Turks?

112
00:12:17,775 --> 00:12:19,840
They are pitting brothers against
brothers.

113
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,715
There are traitors among them, my Bey!

114
00:12:21,975 --> 00:12:24,120
It's obvious that they were tricked by
golds.

115
00:12:24,825 --> 00:12:25,750
But…

116
00:12:26,150 --> 00:12:27,075
Tell me.

117
00:12:28,075 --> 00:12:30,375
Those traitors betrayed their own Bey too.

118
00:12:30,870 --> 00:12:33,950
They killed him and captured his daughter.

119
00:12:34,350 --> 00:12:36,975
Nikola’s men are taking her to the castle
at the moment.

120
00:12:37,775 --> 00:12:39,110
Why did they kill their Bey?

121
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:41,400
Because he refused to fight against us,
my Bey.

122
00:12:45,225 --> 00:12:48,775
Before she enters the pit of Devil, we
must save her.

123
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,425
We are ready, my Bey.

124
00:12:52,850 --> 00:12:55,425
As you can see Bala, it’s not the time
to wait.

125
00:12:56,225 --> 00:12:57,895
You shall go to Tent with Zulfikar.

126
00:12:58,750 --> 00:12:59,975
I won’t wait to fight.

127
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:15,225
My Bala, listen to Selcan Hatun and may
your eyes be wide open.

128
00:13:22,225 --> 00:13:23,200
Let’s go!

129
00:13:46,975 --> 00:13:48,300
Please sit down, my Bey.

130
00:13:51,375 --> 00:13:52,575
You are spinning my head.

131
00:13:53,275 --> 00:13:56,800
They think Osman will do what is said.

132
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:00,125
They are telling me stop.

133
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,875
How can they be this blind?

134
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:06,025
He is becoming worse day by day!

135
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,350
You know he can’t stand Yalvak Arslan.

136
00:14:11,425 --> 00:14:14,525
He loses his mind to his anger whenever
Yalvak is here.

137
00:14:15,875 --> 00:14:18,160
He must be suspecting he’s trying to
deceive us.

138
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:21,060
Is there someone who doesn’t play games in
these lands, Lena?

139
00:14:21,325 --> 00:14:23,025
Perhaps, he has other plans.

140
00:14:25,225 --> 00:14:27,250
He wants the Kayı Tent by his side.

141
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,525
And be sure of Kayı Tent.

142
00:14:29,875 --> 00:14:32,450
Only then, he will cooperate with us.

143
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:36,250
Instead of deceiving us, he wants to
deceive our enemies together.

144
00:14:39,725 --> 00:14:42,925
However, my brother keeps ruining
everything.

145
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:51,800
Is there anything I can do, my Bey?

146
00:14:54,675 --> 00:14:56,200
I’d like to support you.

147
00:14:57,225 --> 00:14:58,900
Keep an eye on Bala Hatun.

148
00:15:02,750 --> 00:15:05,700
Report me every step Selcan and Bala Hatun
will take.

149
00:15:11,950 --> 00:15:15,800
I’m going to stand against everyone who
stand against you.

150
00:15:19,375 --> 00:15:21,625
I will do more things than just
reporting you.

151
00:15:23,550 --> 00:15:25,965
I will control the Hatuns of this Tent
from now on.

152
00:15:29,925 --> 00:15:31,400
How are you going to do that?

153
00:15:33,650 --> 00:15:36,000
Do I ask you how you are managing things?

154
00:15:41,750 --> 00:15:43,675
I will go the Tent of Yalvak Arslan now.

155
00:15:44,675 --> 00:15:45,875
Nobody should know.

156
00:15:46,575 --> 00:15:47,900
Is Osman coming with you?

157
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,025
No.

158
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:51,100
He hasn’t been informed.

159
00:16:12,075 --> 00:16:13,325
How is he doing?

160
00:16:15,475 --> 00:16:16,795
He is burning like a flame.

161
00:16:17,375 --> 00:16:20,275
I sent my Alps to the best physicians.

162
00:16:20,350 --> 00:16:21,875
They will be here soon.

163
00:16:23,025 --> 00:16:26,125
Ertuğrul Bey is like a half-father for me.

164
00:16:26,925 --> 00:16:28,995
I can’t stand seeing him in this
condition.

165
00:16:30,375 --> 00:16:31,800
May Allah bless you.

166
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:35,850
I know how much you like your
brother, Dündar.

167
00:16:37,025 --> 00:16:40,125
I’m aware of your pain and sorrow.

168
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,300
But it’s important to be ready for
everything.

169
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:49,875
It’s haram for us, Beys, to cry after our
loved ones.

170
00:16:54,625 --> 00:16:55,775
What are you saying?

171
00:16:55,825 --> 00:17:02,450
Ertuğrul Bey is not only our loved one but
the one who balances all Tents and powers.

172
00:17:03,750 --> 00:17:06,150
With him, comes the peace.

173
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:11,025
I know how hard it is to replace him.

174
00:17:12,025 --> 00:17:19,375
However, I want you to know that I’ll
stand by your side with this situation.

175
00:17:52,350 --> 00:17:55,350
I’m going to cut your throats once you
open the cage!

176
00:17:56,350 --> 00:17:58,175
You null slaves!

177
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:05,000
Those who dare to fetter lions will be the
victim of claws!

178
00:18:05,075 --> 00:18:06,625
Open the cage!

179
00:18:07,275 --> 00:18:08,500
I said open it!

180
00:18:10,375 --> 00:18:11,600
Open the cage!

181
00:18:40,025 --> 00:18:41,500
Open the cage!

182
00:19:00,950 --> 00:19:03,025
She must be the one Zulfikar told us
about.

183
00:19:07,925 --> 00:19:09,475
Where are they headed, my Bey?

184
00:19:10,375 --> 00:19:11,775
We will learn now.

185
00:19:12,175 --> 00:19:13,225
You stay here.

186
00:19:27,425 --> 00:19:28,450
Stop!

187
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:41,675
Who are you?

188
00:19:43,525 --> 00:19:45,350
Osman, Ertuğrul Gazi’s son.

189
00:19:50,025 --> 00:19:51,200
Set her free.

190
00:19:52,350 --> 00:19:55,125
We were looking for you in the sky but we
found you here.

191
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:07,045
Your sword is sharp, Bey’s daughter.

192
00:22:09,025 --> 00:22:12,050
So you are Osman Bey whom they even
fear you name.

193
00:22:13,025 --> 00:22:14,075
Yes, it’s me.

194
00:22:16,900 --> 00:22:18,955
You didn’t ask but I’ll tell you anyways.

195
00:22:18,955 --> 00:22:19,950
I’m Targun Hatun.

196
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:27,175
What business Kuman Turks have here?

197
00:22:28,650 --> 00:22:30,975
They came here to fight for the Emperor.

198
00:22:30,975 --> 00:22:34,100
They are going to attack you with Nikola
and Flatyos.

199
00:22:35,525 --> 00:22:37,250
From where they will attack?

200
00:22:40,050 --> 00:22:42,335
You need to figure that out yourself,
Osman Bey.

201
00:22:48,950 --> 00:22:50,575
I shall go now.

202
00:22:51,725 --> 00:22:52,725
Stop.

203
00:22:52,975 --> 00:22:53,900
Stop!

204
00:22:58,200 --> 00:23:00,875
You are right. I forgot to thank you.

205
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:03,975
You should thank to Allah, Targun Hatun.

206
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:08,575
Your father was killed as he didn’t want
to attack us.

207
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:13,200
And they caged you because of this reason.

208
00:23:13,625 --> 00:23:16,175
I see you already know everything, Osman
Bey.

209
00:23:16,250 --> 00:23:17,750
What else do you want from me?

210
00:23:20,375 --> 00:23:22,725
Your life is an escrow for us from now on.

211
00:23:23,550 --> 00:23:25,750
I can guard my life by my own, Osman Bey.

212
00:23:26,225 --> 00:23:27,875
You shouldn’t bother.

213
00:23:28,375 --> 00:23:30,400
I don’t have the time to argue!

214
00:23:30,975 --> 00:23:32,375
Listen to my words!

215
00:23:33,525 --> 00:23:34,850
We should go to the Tent.

216
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:42,150
Though our religions are different, we
both come from Oghuz lineage.

217
00:23:42,550 --> 00:23:43,825
You are right, Osman Bey.

218
00:23:44,325 --> 00:23:46,100
Our veins share the same blood.

219
00:23:52,125 --> 00:23:53,450
You will be our guest.

220
00:23:54,825 --> 00:23:57,465
Also, you have a wound which needs to be
taken care of.

221
00:23:57,650 --> 00:23:58,950
Nothing but a scratch.

222
00:23:58,975 --> 00:24:00,600
It needs to be stigmatized.

223
00:24:05,225 --> 00:24:06,250
Let’s go.

224
00:24:39,525 --> 00:24:40,775
Valiants!

225
00:24:43,050 --> 00:24:47,050
From now on, you can’t take a break to
drink water.

226
00:24:47,750 --> 00:24:50,450
Not even to breath!

227
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:58,475
Your swords should be sharp so that they
can kill forty soldiers with one swing!

228
00:24:59,825 --> 00:25:01,025
Come on, Valiants!

229
00:25:01,275 --> 00:25:06,075
You are not allowed to make mistakes!

230
00:25:26,525 --> 00:25:29,125
Stand straight!

231
00:25:30,425 --> 00:25:32,150
May your steps be strong!

232
00:25:32,475 --> 00:25:35,275
The time of many battles has come!

233
00:25:36,070 --> 00:25:39,375
Yeah, just like this!

234
00:25:41,325 --> 00:25:45,325
We must execute even the easiest
task with such care!

235
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:46,675
Go now!

236
00:25:47,225 --> 00:25:49,650
Do you all understand?

237
00:25:49,850 --> 00:25:51,615
-Yes, our Bey!
-Don't worry, our Bey!

238
00:25:52,175 --> 00:25:57,600
My Bey, as you ordered, we surrounded the
Tent with a huge wall made out of spears.

239
00:25:58,350 --> 00:26:00,800
With Allah's permisson, even a fly
can't breach it.

240
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:02,500
Thank you, my Ayaz.

241
00:26:02,925 --> 00:26:08,450
You should also remove all the bridges
there are on the ditches.

242
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:12,750
After all, even a single mistake can bring
the end of our Tent.

243
00:26:12,950 --> 00:26:14,150
Go now, Valiant.

244
00:26:14,350 --> 00:26:15,575
As you order, my Bey.

245
00:26:17,175 --> 00:26:22,175
Bamsı Bey, the archers are on their
position and we doubled their numbers.

246
00:26:22,170 --> 00:26:25,450
How wonderful, my lion Valiant!

247
00:26:25,650 --> 00:26:27,325
Go to your position now.

248
00:26:31,850 --> 00:26:35,575
How magnificent!

249
00:26:46,075 --> 00:26:47,275
Do you like your place?

250
00:26:48,675 --> 00:26:50,125
I think it’s pretty good.

251
00:26:54,250 --> 00:26:57,850
Nikola, Osman has just saved Targun Hatun.

252
00:26:59,450 --> 00:27:03,300
He is Osman and he is capable of doing
such things.

253
00:27:04,725 --> 00:27:06,125
He’s taking her to the Tent.

254
00:27:08,625 --> 00:27:11,750
Wouldn’t you do the same thing if you
were him, Flatyos?

255
00:27:12,925 --> 00:27:14,175
You know what they say.

256
00:27:14,825 --> 00:27:17,875
Osman took the bait.

257
00:27:21,170 --> 00:27:23,875
Open your eyes wide open.

258
00:27:34,975 --> 00:27:37,450
I heard you need our help, Nikola.

259
00:27:37,550 --> 00:27:39,450
So, after all, the Emperor sent you?

260
00:27:40,350 --> 00:27:42,575
He knows we fight better than the Romans.

261
00:27:43,280 --> 00:27:47,160
He sent his best units.
Looks like he believes in you.

262
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:51,240
You must be their
leader since he sent you.

263
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:53,480
Have no doubt.

264
00:27:53,480 --> 00:28:02,840
Targun. You and Kayıs share ancestors, you
wouldn't also act like them, would you?

265
00:28:02,840 --> 00:28:08,640
Don't worry, Nikola. We're used
to doing what the Romans can't.

266
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:14,440
This duty is more
dangerous than before.

267
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:28,200
Are you having fun?

268
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:32,080
As long as you're in my arms like this,
I'd always have fun.

269
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:37,600
If you don't free my father immediately,
your life will be hell!

270
00:28:38,360 --> 00:28:44,640
I'll free your father
if you can complete your duty.

271
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:49,960
- What duty?
- Prisoner duty.

272
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:58,080
- Who will I capture?
- Yourself. You'll be like your father.

273
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:02,320
I'm used to working with my sword.

274
00:29:02,320 --> 00:29:12,400
Your mind is as sharp as your sword.
I want the Kayıs to know that.

275
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:22,920
Mighty Ceasar.
This is our first step.

276
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:47,320
It'The time for revenge
is close, father!

277
00:29:47,320 --> 00:29:53,120
Hazal...
You'll pay for what you've done!

278
00:29:57,560 --> 00:30:02,200
I’ve decided to wait for Aygül to be okay…

279
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:05,760
… and not tell anyone while doing it.

280
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:12,240
But I had to come after
hearing about Ertuğrul Bey.

281
00:30:24,520 --> 00:30:26,040
Bala?

282
00:30:28,080 --> 00:30:29,840
Bala, my daughter.

283
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:33,800
Are you okay?

284
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:39,480
You’re really inspecting those carpets.

285
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:43,920
Nothing. I’m just daydreaming.

286
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:49,680
If you don’t let it out,
your troubles will grow on the inside.

287
00:30:49,680 --> 00:30:51,800
Tell your mother about it.

288
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:55,920
I’m worrying about Osman, mother.

289
00:30:57,880 --> 00:31:00,000
What about Osman?

290
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,920
He went to rescue a woman.

291
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:05,280
What’s wrong with that?

292
00:31:10,040 --> 00:31:14,520
Shouldn’t every valiant
fight for the good of the poor?

293
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:18,040
That’s right.

294
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:22,320
But there’s something in my heart.

295
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:35,320
I’ll come another time.

296
00:31:35,320 --> 00:31:37,320
It’s okay, daughter.

297
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:41,280
Is he sleeping?

298
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,400
Mashallah!

299
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:57,880
What is that for?

300
00:31:59,360 --> 00:32:02,480
You go, Selcan mother.
I’ll look after the baby.

301
00:32:02,480 --> 00:32:04,520
Thank you.

302
00:32:45,320 --> 00:32:47,320
Welcome my Bey.

303
00:32:55,240 --> 00:32:57,160
Welcome my Bey.

304
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:02,480
Welcome my Bey.

305
00:33:28,760 --> 00:33:31,240
We have company.

306
00:33:53,800 --> 00:33:56,240
Just a guest.

307
00:34:28,120 --> 00:34:29,679
Aunt.

308
00:34:30,639 --> 00:34:32,480
My valiant!

309
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:36,719
Glad you came. We couldn’t
find time to chat with you.

310
00:34:36,719 --> 00:34:39,440
We’ll eventually do it, son.

311
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:51,719
Who’s this lady?

312
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:56,560
Daughter of a
Bey running away from cruelty.

313
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:07,040
Welcome. Don’t feel like a guest. You’re
one of us now. Feel like our daughter.

314
00:35:07,560 --> 00:35:12,720
Thank you. I know how
hospitable Kayıs are.

315
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:23,160
You’ve rescued a prisoner.
Give me a tent and I’ll support you too.

316
00:35:30,600 --> 00:35:37,120
Bala. Take care of our guest.
She’s wounded.

317
00:35:37,120 --> 00:35:39,120
Of course, my Bey.

318
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:48,480
Aunt.

319
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:05,000
Such a guest won’t
leave so easily, my Bala.

320
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:20,240
I’ve something to tell you.

321
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:23,600
I wonder what it is. Tell me, son.

322
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:27,520
She’s our guest. But…

323
00:36:28,760 --> 00:36:31,160
… keep your eye on her.

324
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:38,080
Are you suspicious of something.

325
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:41,320
Being suspicious is a must for me, aunt.

326
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:48,680
It is indeed. Don’t worry.
I’ll take care of her.

327
00:36:48,680 --> 00:36:51,280
Thank you.

328
00:36:57,520 --> 00:37:00,480
My Bey! News from Kumral Abdal.

329
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:02,280
What is it?

330
00:37:03,600 --> 00:37:05,720
They found Cerkutay’s trace.

331
00:37:05,920 --> 00:37:07,760
Cerkutay!

332
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:10,920
They saw them running away
from Nökers near İnegöl.

333
00:37:11,640 --> 00:37:17,880
Get him immediately. So that we can
see what tricks they’re playing.

334
00:37:18,760 --> 00:37:21,000
Okay, my Bey.

335
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,280
Cerkutay!

336
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:11,920
No one will be able to save you from me.

337
00:38:14,560 --> 00:38:17,680
It is time to pay, Hazal!

338
00:38:22,880 --> 00:38:25,600
It is time to pay!

339
00:39:13,800 --> 00:39:22,080
I’m waiting for Ertuğrul Bey to open his
eyes like I’m waiting for some good news.

340
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:33,720
I can’t wait for him to open his eyes
and say “Abdurrahman! Be ready!”.

341
00:39:35,160 --> 00:39:39,160
But our Bey’s state isn’t good.

342
00:39:41,520 --> 00:39:46,680
If it was someone else,
he’d be dead by now.

343
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:55,120
I think he has something left to do
since he’s fighting death for us.

344
00:39:58,560 --> 00:40:06,000
My mighty Bey!
He won’t give up so easily.

345
00:40:06,840 --> 00:40:11,240
He has things to do
and battles to fight.

346
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:17,960
Friends! Duties don’t wait,
battles don’t end!

347
00:40:18,280 --> 00:40:24,560
You don’t oppose
the act of Allah!

348
00:40:27,160 --> 00:40:32,880
Lives are temporary. You don’t
complain while giving them back.

349
00:40:40,840 --> 00:40:44,680
Kayı Tent is under control
of those who support Yavlak.

350
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:49,760
While my father is fighting for his life…

351
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:55,160
... Kayı’s cause is humiliated
by a fool named Yavlak.

352
00:40:59,480 --> 00:41:02,720
Dündar Bey is Ertuğrul Bey’s brother.

353
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:06,800
Gündüz and Savcı Bey are their sons.

354
00:41:07,560 --> 00:41:11,240
They won’t pursue this
mistake, Inshallah.

355
00:41:14,960 --> 00:41:18,280
I’ll bring them back from this mistake.

356
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:29,240
May it be easy.

357
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:54,120
Our Hatuns are quite skilled.

358
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:05,320
Fine craftsmanship.

359
00:42:20,480 --> 00:42:26,600
Why are you all around the guest?
You should let her breathe.

360
00:42:28,760 --> 00:42:33,600
Bala. Our guest’s wound
needs to be seared.

361
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:37,760
- I can do that!
- Bala will do it.

362
00:42:38,840 --> 00:42:41,680
You can take care of Ertuğrul Bey.

363
00:42:46,120 --> 00:42:48,680
Don’t worry, mother.

364
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:53,800
I’ve heard about Kayı carpets.
I could finally see them.

365
00:42:53,800 --> 00:43:00,200
Mashallah! Our name is heard
all the way from there!

366
00:43:03,480 --> 00:43:08,120
Bala. The wound
doesn’t wait. Let’s go.

367
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:27,480
Osman hunted
a deer this time.

368
00:43:38,280 --> 00:43:40,360
The end is near.

369
00:43:40,720 --> 00:43:48,400
When it takes place, I want
you all to hear my decision.

370
00:43:51,280 --> 00:43:57,480
Know it, so that you can act accordingly.

371
00:44:13,240 --> 00:44:21,120
When Ertuğrul Gazi, son
of Süleiman Şah, passes away…

372
00:44:22,880 --> 00:44:30,480
… the throne of Beys, as his son…

373
00:44:33,320 --> 00:44:35,200
… will be mine.

374
00:44:42,800 --> 00:44:45,120
I’d die for you!

375
00:44:51,960 --> 00:44:56,240
From now on, hogs like Geyhatu…

376
00:44:57,200 --> 00:44:59,280
… rabid dogs like Nikola…

377
00:45:00,120 --> 00:45:05,080
… degenerates like Yavlak won’t
be standing in our way.

378
00:45:08,560 --> 00:45:14,640
Eyvallah, Osman. The castle we
conquered is on the enemy’s hands.

379
00:45:16,040 --> 00:45:21,400
People will remind you that.

380
00:45:24,840 --> 00:45:29,280
We need to take Kulacahisar.

381
00:45:31,800 --> 00:45:36,600
You can then announce
the decision you’ve made here.

382
00:45:43,640 --> 00:45:46,000
I’ll enter that castle.

383
00:45:50,560 --> 00:45:54,040
If my brothers and
uncle divided Kayı…

384
00:45:54,640 --> 00:45:58,240
… if I don’t have enough Alps
to reconquer that castle…

385
00:45:58,640 --> 00:46:05,560
… then I’ll infiltrate the castle and
cut the throats of Nikola and Flatyos!

386
00:46:07,560 --> 00:46:10,680
Osman! We don’t doubt that.

387
00:46:10,680 --> 00:46:17,040
But if you’re going to be a Bey,
you shouldn’t put yourself in danger.

388
00:46:17,560 --> 00:46:22,480
Don’t act before learning
what Savcı thinks.

389
00:46:26,160 --> 00:46:31,000
I worry that you’ll
trip each other.

390
00:46:32,560 --> 00:46:35,400
Where are my brothers and uncle?

391
00:46:37,560 --> 00:46:42,560
Tell me. Why should we care about
what they think if they’re not here?

392
00:46:43,320 --> 00:46:46,920
Your brothers and uncle
are in Yavlak Arslan’s pavilion.

393
00:46:50,040 --> 00:46:53,240
They’re celebrating the Bey of the Beys.

394
00:46:57,200 --> 00:46:59,400
What are you saying, Bamsı Bey?

395
00:47:01,040 --> 00:47:02,800
Why didn’t you tell me?

396
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:06,480
Because they’re doing
something behind your back.

397
00:47:06,480 --> 00:47:10,280
I didn’t want you to
do something out of anger.

398
00:47:11,120 --> 00:47:13,480
They’re doing things
behind my back.

399
00:47:14,120 --> 00:47:19,760
Are those who Ertuğrul Gazi’s
successors are?

400
00:47:20,360 --> 00:47:23,240
Are those who will
protect Kayı’s future?

401
00:47:26,280 --> 00:47:28,640
They visited Yavlak Arslan personally!

402
00:47:28,640 --> 00:47:33,240
Son, they made a mistake.
They’ll eventually correct it!

403
00:47:34,720 --> 00:47:40,000
- I’ll show them.
- Son! What will you show them?

404
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:42,580
One of them is your uncle,
the rest are your brothers!

405
00:47:42,580 --> 00:47:44,200
Don’t make a mistake!

406
00:47:44,400 --> 00:47:51,000
Bamsı Bey! Make up your mind!

407
00:47:53,560 --> 00:47:57,880
Are you with me or not?

408
00:47:59,920 --> 00:48:07,280
My dark-eyed Osman!

409
00:48:08,560 --> 00:48:13,600
Being by your side doesn’t
mean supporting your mistakes!

410
00:48:14,600 --> 00:48:19,240
Of course, we’re with you.

411
00:48:19,240 --> 00:48:27,600
But it is our duty to warn you when
you’re this close to making mistakes!

412
00:48:28,480 --> 00:48:34,360
We got these manners from
our ancestors, remember?

413
00:48:46,040 --> 00:48:51,720
The age of brothers and uncles are over!

414
00:48:52,800 --> 00:48:55,360
Following one’s feelings is over!

415
00:48:57,520 --> 00:49:00,360
It’s time to be a state!

416
00:49:01,560 --> 00:49:05,320
No one will be able
to stand against this cause!

417
00:49:05,960 --> 00:49:08,800
Everyone will show their faces!

418
00:49:09,200 --> 00:49:12,080
No one can be a Mongol and a Kayı!

419
00:49:12,520 --> 00:49:15,560
No one can be a Greek and a Turk!

420
00:49:16,240 --> 00:49:19,400
There can be no war and peace!

421
00:49:20,400 --> 00:49:23,600
Either Turk or Mongol!

422
00:49:24,080 --> 00:49:27,400
Either Kayı or Greek!

423
00:49:28,520 --> 00:49:33,920
Either blasphemy or faith!

424
00:49:51,520 --> 00:49:53,600
Mashallah!

425
00:50:18,400 --> 00:50:20,000
It will hurt.

426
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:21,400
I don’t want it.

427
00:51:55,040 --> 00:51:59,560
With the seal and
the duty we’ve received…

428
00:51:59,560 --> 00:52:02,240
… we’ve our responsibilities increased.

429
00:52:03,480 --> 00:52:10,960
We’ll all be relaxing if we
succeed in our responsibilities.

430
00:52:10,960 --> 00:52:17,520
We’ll be free of
the Mongol’s punishments.

431
00:52:18,200 --> 00:52:23,920
We’ve wasted our people
and resources in these campaigns.

432
00:52:25,200 --> 00:52:31,040
Now, we need to
enter an age of peace.

433
00:52:32,320 --> 00:52:41,280
As you know, the leader of Kayı’s Ertuğrul
Bey, who share borders with the greeks…

434
00:52:41,280 --> 00:52:46,200
… is fighting for his life
against a deadly disease.

435
00:52:47,280 --> 00:52:50,000
He’s in no shape to make decisions.

436
00:52:54,200 --> 00:53:02,480
Savcı Bey, with Ertuğrul Bey’s order,
is the leader of Kayı Tent.

437
00:53:10,880 --> 00:53:18,640
Beys of Kayı shall obey Savcı
like they obey Ertuğrul Gazi.

438
00:53:19,320 --> 00:53:23,920
I don’t see Osman and Bamsı Bey here.

439
00:53:23,920 --> 00:53:28,720
This seems like an
attitude against Savcı Bey.

440
00:53:29,480 --> 00:53:35,200
Under these circumstances,
how will peace be established?

441
00:53:41,240 --> 00:53:48,560
I asked Osman and
Bamsı Bey to not be here.

442
00:53:50,080 --> 00:53:54,720
Neither of them will have
anything left in Kayı Tent.

443
00:54:01,880 --> 00:54:12,800
Osman Bey is mad. But he’ll see
that resisting alone is not the way.

444
00:54:16,960 --> 00:54:24,320
If we work together,
what can he do?

445
00:54:24,320 --> 00:54:28,400
If Bamsı Bey is with him,
he’s not alone.

446
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:31,360
That means he has an army!

447
00:54:32,520 --> 00:54:38,400
Osman Bey is an army on his own!

448
00:54:42,560 --> 00:54:50,960
Bamsı Bey is valiant. But he’s old.

449
00:54:52,120 --> 00:54:57,760
Bamsı Bey doesn’t have
a place in the future of Kayı.

450
00:55:07,280 --> 00:55:12,880
My brother Osman
wants the good of Kayıs.

451
00:55:13,720 --> 00:55:17,600
He wants them to grow and expand.

452
00:55:18,120 --> 00:55:20,760
Remember, Beys.

453
00:55:21,600 --> 00:55:27,600
He was victorious many times.
He conquered Kulacahisar.

454
00:55:40,600 --> 00:55:42,440
But…

455
00:55:43,440 --> 00:55:49,240
But he also saw that conquests
without solid foundations are no good.

456
00:55:55,160 --> 00:55:58,400
He’ll see that you can’t
found states in one day.

457
00:55:58,640 --> 00:56:00,920
- Inshallah.
- Inshallah.

458
00:56:05,920 --> 00:56:13,760
He has to. We have
to be together for greater goals!

459
00:56:13,760 --> 00:56:17,680
I’ll set off for Kastamonu today.

460
00:56:18,360 --> 00:56:21,100
I want to see that I’m leaving
something strong behind.

461
00:56:21,100 --> 00:56:22,320
I’m counting on you.

462
00:57:16,160 --> 00:57:21,680
Kongar! Brother! I knew you’d come back!

463
00:57:23,120 --> 00:57:26,280
Göktuğ, not Kongar!

464
00:57:26,280 --> 00:57:30,640
Your death, not your brother!

465
00:57:31,600 --> 00:57:34,640
You didn’t come from me?

466
00:57:36,760 --> 00:57:38,920
Pity.

467
00:58:00,080 --> 00:58:02,440
Death, you were saying?

468
00:58:02,880 --> 00:58:08,600
Death is here, Kongar.
But not for me! For you!

469
00:58:26,560 --> 00:58:28,640
What do we have here?

470
00:58:28,640 --> 00:58:30,640
What are you doing
here, Flatyos?

471
00:58:31,040 --> 00:58:35,200
Göktuğ is also here.
We had some accounts for calling.

472
00:58:35,200 --> 00:58:39,480
It won’t take long,
Flatyos! Don’t worry!

473
00:58:45,604 --> 00:58:49,333
I congratulate you for becoming
the Bey of Beys...

474
00:58:50,840 --> 00:58:58,633
...but, won't there be anything done for
Kulucahisar before you return to Kastamonu?

475
00:59:01,287 --> 00:59:04,835
Will Nicola the dishonorable
go unpunished?

476
00:59:08,274 --> 00:59:11,771
Let's say that Osman Bey is rushing,
he is unwary...

477
00:59:12,397 --> 00:59:14,965
...then, what is the measure
you are taking?

478
00:59:16,537 --> 00:59:20,580
When do you want to take the castle?

479
00:59:21,254 --> 00:59:27,780
It will wait. Now, nothing will be done
without Geyhatu's approval.

480
00:59:28,620 --> 00:59:32,364
Of course, we'll take Kulucahisar back.
What do you think?

481
00:59:32,689 --> 00:59:40,242
Yavlak Arslan has great targets.
What is Kulucahisar? If you don't defy me...

482
00:59:40,574 --> 00:59:45,690
...if you follow me with your
alps in war-time...

483
00:59:46,068 --> 00:59:49,874
...I can take even Bursa and İznik.

484
00:59:56,057 --> 01:00:02,423
It will be that way, surely.
The dark days will be gone.

485
01:00:08,289 --> 01:00:13,345
As long as we move with caution,
we can take both İznik and Bursa.

486
01:00:21,218 --> 01:00:22,879
Surely, we can.

487
01:00:40,286 --> 01:00:44,680
Bamsı Bey, we have orders.
Osman Bey won't be taken to the meeting.

488
01:00:53,088 --> 01:00:55,167
I will enter if I want to.

489
01:00:59,479 --> 01:01:02,211
Don't worry about Osman anymore.

490
01:01:04,480 --> 01:01:06,097
Open the door!

491
01:01:08,378 --> 01:01:10,976
Don't make me kill you.

492
01:01:30,374 --> 01:01:36,078
You forgot Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman
Bey, and the great ghazi Bamsı Bey.

493
01:01:38,120 --> 01:01:46,931
Osman! You went over your level again,
Osman! You violated the law again!

494
01:01:48,129 --> 01:01:56,765
The laws? The enemy is sending the Cuman
cavalries upon us to make Turks...

495
01:01:57,516 --> 01:02:03,833
...kill Turks, and you are here sitting
and eating. Is this the law?

496
01:02:04,352 --> 01:02:11,343
-How do you know that?
-How do I know? I heard and confirmed it.

497
01:02:24,896 --> 01:02:28,027
We will penetrate them, brother.
That's a bad ambush.

498
01:02:28,720 --> 01:02:29,881
Attack!

499
01:02:31,489 --> 01:02:32,421
Come on!

500
01:02:48,926 --> 01:02:49,895
Wait!

501
01:02:57,879 --> 01:03:02,679
We got our hunt.
We can take care of them later.

502
01:03:39,902 --> 01:03:42,954
What does this dog Flatyos have
to do with Cerkutay?

503
01:03:43,509 --> 01:03:49,620
Osman Bey will get mad, brother. Cerkutay
was a link to everything and we lost him.

504
01:03:52,430 --> 01:03:59,634
While you are sitting here, the enemy is
preparing to strike the Kayı Tribe.

505
01:04:04,410 --> 01:04:05,410
Alps.

506
01:04:10,916 --> 01:04:12,631
Hold there!

507
01:04:13,441 --> 01:04:20,424
Bamsı Bey! Do you know what does it mean
to draw a sword in the Bey of Beys' presence?

508
01:04:21,096 --> 01:04:26,886
Bamsı Bey! You are stepping over us all.

509
01:04:30,844 --> 01:04:32,043
Uncle!

510
01:04:38,659 --> 01:04:40,289
Brothers!

511
01:04:42,635 --> 01:04:46,771
This is the end of words.
It's time for a decision now.

512
01:04:49,470 --> 01:04:54,534
You'll either stand with this Yavlak who
hides under the dresses of the Mongols...

513
01:04:54,639 --> 01:04:58,983
...who work together with the heathens
that are the greatest enemies of the Turks!

514
01:05:00,736 --> 01:05:08,224
Or, you will stand with me, who fights for
the holy war, who can't be stopped...

515
01:05:08,605 --> 01:05:18,171
...with chains, who rathers die than
getting captured; Osman Bey!

516
01:05:29,567 --> 01:05:33,267
Make your decision and pay the cost.

517
01:05:40,773 --> 01:05:44,802
And about that Yavlak Arslan that
you sit at his table...

518
01:05:46,698 --> 01:05:49,609
...I will expose him as well.

519
01:05:55,961 --> 01:05:59,669
He'll pay for the ravens he sent after me.

520
01:06:00,007 --> 01:06:07,558
Osman, know your words.
You don't have any evidence...

521
01:06:07,558 --> 01:06:08,930
Enough!

522
01:06:13,253 --> 01:06:15,909
How much more will you defy me, Osman?

523
01:06:16,841 --> 01:06:21,229
No one will be able to stand against
the state that I will build!

524
01:06:21,903 --> 01:06:23,516
What state?

525
01:06:27,762 --> 01:06:30,038
What state, Osman?

526
01:06:45,566 --> 01:06:49,575
The state of those who bow down to
no one but Allah...

527
01:06:51,169 --> 01:06:57,825
...who don't listen to no Mongol no Rum
nor anyone else when it's about...

528
01:06:58,410 --> 01:07:02,653
...the future, the freedom of the Turks!
Who believe in Allah...

529
01:07:03,122 --> 01:07:07,223
...who seeks the holy war, who sharpen
their blade with their faith...

530
01:07:08,317 --> 01:07:18,528
...who says that 'If we are here, there is
hope for the oppressed'!

531
01:07:30,386 --> 01:07:33,355
Not Shepherd's son Yavlak Arslan's!

532
01:07:36,854 --> 01:07:42,897
The state of those who come after
Oghuz Khan's most noble son Gün Khan's...

533
01:07:43,437 --> 01:07:47,943
... most noble son Kayı's lineage!

534
01:08:03,062 --> 01:08:08,848
I love you, brother.
Make your decision. Don't face me.

535
01:08:41,012 --> 01:08:45,712
Did you do it? Where is Cerkutay?

536
01:08:49,627 --> 01:08:51,783
Where is Cerkutay?

537
01:08:53,630 --> 01:08:59,173
My bey, we took the dog from the Mongols.
We were bringing him to you but...

538
01:08:59,173 --> 01:09:00,693
...Flatyos showed up.

539
01:09:00,994 --> 01:09:04,224
-Where did Flatyos come from?
-They were so many, my bey...

540
01:09:05,447 --> 01:09:07,010
...we were ambushed.

541
01:09:08,829 --> 01:09:11,716
Ahh, lads. Ahh, lads.

542
01:09:12,364 --> 01:09:14,532
What does Flatyos have to do with
Cerkutay?

543
01:09:14,733 --> 01:09:17,686
Calm down, son. You can't solve it
with this anger.

544
01:09:20,662 --> 01:09:25,677
If Nicola is behind this, it means that
they are united.

545
01:09:26,927 --> 01:09:29,875
Time gets narrowed, enemies
come together...

546
01:09:31,974 --> 01:09:33,845
...and we divide.

547
01:10:12,303 --> 01:10:17,830
Cerkutay is here and this is our
second move, Flatyos.

548
01:10:24,314 --> 01:10:29,058
I took him from Osman's alps,
not the Mongols.

549
01:10:29,478 --> 01:10:35,117
This is even better, Flatyos.
So, Osman too is after Cerkutay.

550
01:10:36,244 --> 01:10:39,309
His alps returned empty-handed, then.

551
01:10:39,789 --> 01:10:45,823
-Indeed, Nikola.
-Good. Osman must be mad now.

552
01:10:46,676 --> 01:10:49,846
He is coming to the point that I want.

553
01:11:03,549 --> 01:11:09,741
Tell me, Cerkutay. Who was behind
the raven that set a trap for Osman?

554
01:11:21,452 --> 01:11:22,629
Who knows?

555
01:11:29,301 --> 01:11:34,788
You. You know it, Cerkutay. Come.

556
01:11:46,138 --> 01:11:47,213
Shhh...

557
01:11:52,545 --> 01:12:00,033
Look, we can do it this way too if you like.
I can make you talk in Roman ways.

558
01:12:04,688 --> 01:12:06,741
Do it in Mongol ways.

559
01:12:27,214 --> 01:12:30,119
Who was behind the trap?

560
01:12:32,423 --> 01:12:33,994
Who was it?

561
01:12:33,994 --> 01:12:35,793
Yavlak Arslan is coming, sir.

562
01:12:38,729 --> 01:12:44,204
-What is Yavlak Arslan doing here?
-We'll see, Nicola.

563
01:12:52,055 --> 01:12:55,987
Take this Mongol dog, bring my guest.

564
01:13:27,849 --> 01:13:32,017
Flatyos, why are you never happy?

565
01:13:34,222 --> 01:13:41,453
The soldiers that I asked from the emperor
is here. What are we waiting for?

566
01:13:41,735 --> 01:13:48,379
Flatyos, you want us to raid a place every day,
fight with Kayıs, with Yavlak Arslan every day.

567
01:13:48,379 --> 01:13:54,558
That only happens in tales. States stay
alive with the minds of smart people.

568
01:13:58,303 --> 01:14:05,300
Putting your trust in a Cuman woman
doesn't sound so smart to me, Nicola.

569
01:14:10,773 --> 01:14:13,058
Flatyos...

570
01:14:18,379 --> 01:14:26,043
Flatyos, she will only do as we say and
make Kayı Tribe less habitable. That's all.

571
01:14:26,467 --> 01:14:33,227
Enraged Osman will come to our foot, we won't
go to him. He will come to us, do you understand?

572
01:14:33,641 --> 01:14:40,787
Then, we will crush him like stepping over a bug.
Then we will enter the defenseless Söğüt.

573
01:14:41,460 --> 01:14:42,940
Do you get it?

574
01:14:43,134 --> 01:14:46,621
I like tactics.

575
01:16:00,418 --> 01:16:04,446
Thank you.
You are helpful, just like Osman Bey.

576
01:16:05,954 --> 01:16:10,944
Osman Bey is like that.
He helps every oppressed he sees.

577
01:16:11,524 --> 01:16:12,793
He is a valiant man.

578
01:16:15,394 --> 01:16:16,718
He is.

579
01:16:31,392 --> 01:16:33,906
What's wrong, I wonder?

580
01:16:34,682 --> 01:16:36,701
Did you get lost, Hazal?

581
01:16:48,326 --> 01:16:53,208
What was your intention in bringing
Aygül back to the tents?

582
01:16:53,929 --> 01:16:58,324
It's Aygül's tribe. She returned
to her home.

583
01:17:01,255 --> 01:17:05,003
So, you are sure that she won't
do anything crazy?

584
01:17:06,182 --> 01:17:09,078
You should've thought that before
driving her crazy.

585
01:17:09,986 --> 01:17:13,178
You made her crazy, I healed her.

586
01:17:14,093 --> 01:17:20,984
Why did you bring that child? Won't Dündar
Bey go mad when he sees that child?

587
01:17:22,596 --> 01:17:25,092
Won't he go crazy this time?

588
01:17:27,773 --> 01:17:34,346
What can we do?
Everyone will pay for what they did, Hazal.

589
01:17:39,573 --> 01:17:40,331
Come on.

590
01:17:58,531 --> 01:17:59,729
Aygül.

591
01:18:16,823 --> 01:18:20,369
I came to finish what was
left unfinished, Hazal.

592
01:18:28,779 --> 01:18:34,660
Aygül, enough. Listen to me, you promised me.
You told me that you won't.

593
01:18:34,885 --> 01:18:37,235
-Get out of my way!
-I'm talking to you, Aygül.

594
01:18:38,490 --> 01:18:41,361
You promised me, lower your sword,
my girl.

595
01:18:41,935 --> 01:18:43,675
Lower your sword, my girl.

596
01:18:44,009 --> 01:18:46,481
She killed my mother!

597
01:18:48,291 --> 01:18:51,466
-Aygül, enough! Enough, my girl.
-Get out of my way!

598
01:18:53,978 --> 01:18:56,426
What did you promise me, Aygül?

599
01:19:09,244 --> 01:19:10,945
I should go and check what's going on.

600
01:19:10,945 --> 01:19:12,646
Go, go, don't worry about me.

601
01:19:44,791 --> 01:19:47,775
I'm in your tent from the first day,
Osman Bey.

602
01:19:52,638 --> 01:19:55,276
Stop! Stop!

603
01:20:01,588 --> 01:20:03,540
Aygül, Aygül! I said stop!

604
01:20:04,105 --> 01:20:06,034
Hazal, Hazal, stop!

605
01:20:11,041 --> 01:20:13,831
Do you want to die? I trained her!

606
01:21:20,693 --> 01:21:22,589
This is the end, Hazal.

607
01:21:37,577 --> 01:21:40,023
-Enough!
-Let me go! Let me go!

608
01:21:40,551 --> 01:21:43,085
Give me that. Take her.

609
01:21:44,359 --> 01:21:46,387
I said, let me go!

610
01:21:50,385 --> 01:21:52,692
It's not the end!

611
01:21:54,417 --> 01:21:58,567
I will kill you and the ones
who saved you!

612
01:22:09,198 --> 01:22:12,637
It's not the end! It's not the end!

613
01:22:18,981 --> 01:22:21,966
How bad can a tribe go?

614
01:22:25,467 --> 01:22:28,686
O' traveler. Where do you head to?

615
01:22:29,540 --> 01:22:32,406
To the Red Apple.
(the idea of Turkic expansionism)

616
01:22:32,879 --> 01:22:35,912
How happy the travelers of that path,
the ones who sharpen their blades with faith.

617
01:22:36,912 --> 01:22:40,792
How happy the ones who ride
their horses in the dawn.

618
01:22:41,846 --> 01:22:42,846
O' expecter!

619
01:22:43,866 --> 01:22:50,602
Say it, for the blades that shine under
the dark of night! For the cities...

620
01:22:50,602 --> 01:22:54,602
...that set fire by the speed of
our horses!

621
01:22:55,868 --> 01:22:58,177
Which way is the Red Apple?

622
01:24:18,187 --> 01:24:19,907
What is the difference...

623
01:24:20,537 --> 01:24:22,927
between day and nigh, Osman Bey?

624
01:24:24,240 --> 01:24:28,800
In Kayı Tribe...

625
01:24:31,266 --> 01:24:33,366
It's always been night lately.

626
01:24:34,852 --> 01:24:36,512
What is the reason?

627
01:24:38,830 --> 01:24:41,440
Kayı's sun is sinking.

628
01:24:44,350 --> 01:24:47,380
Death is at Our Bey Ertugrul Ghazi's door.

629
01:24:47,919 --> 01:24:53,349
Is this the reason there is chaos?

630
01:24:53,599 --> 01:24:59,889
Is this the reason nobody helps each other?

631
01:25:00,422 --> 01:25:04,652
Brothers help each other.

632
01:25:05,132 --> 01:25:06,482
They keep in touch.

633
01:25:11,605 --> 01:25:16,815
- They don't know.
- What do you know, Osman Bey?

634
01:25:18,362 --> 01:25:20,762
What is your aim?

635
01:25:22,413 --> 01:25:24,893
I'll take what we lost back.

636
01:25:26,456 --> 01:25:31,146
I'll punish the wild enemy.

637
01:25:32,413 --> 01:25:39,203
I'll fight the enemy with my Alps who
want The Red Apple.

638
01:25:41,412 --> 01:25:43,172
Until...

639
01:25:44,518 --> 01:25:50,338
Until we become a state.
Our children shall see it.

640
01:25:51,854 --> 01:25:55,854
They shall broaden their perspective.

641
01:25:59,674 --> 01:26:01,464
Thank you.

642
01:26:02,192 --> 01:26:07,242
May Allah help you.

643
01:26:08,403 --> 01:26:12,973
You shall clash the enemy with your Alps..

644
01:26:12,991 --> 01:26:16,781
who want The Red Apple.

645
01:26:17,336 --> 01:26:21,896
When you rise your flag...

646
01:26:21,905 --> 01:26:25,795
Noble Turks shall be with you.

647
01:26:27,246 --> 01:26:28,506
Amin.

648
01:26:30,680 --> 01:26:36,641
Osman Bey, your duty is difficult.

649
01:26:36,641 --> 01:26:38,571
Don't give up.

650
01:26:38,744 --> 01:26:42,074
Your duty is full of enemies.

651
01:26:42,521 --> 01:26:44,341
Don't turn your back.

652
01:26:45,585 --> 01:26:50,425
Your intention will enlight your way.

653
01:26:51,482 --> 01:26:53,852
Don't give up.

654
01:26:59,007 --> 01:27:03,267
May Allah help you.

655
01:27:04,412 --> 01:27:05,742
Amin.

656
01:27:17,754 --> 01:27:19,974
What are those Kuman troops about?

657
01:27:20,335 --> 01:27:24,966
Yavlak. I thought we'd celebrate you being
Bey of the Beys.

658
01:27:24,966 --> 01:27:28,296
You took Kulucahisar.
What are you still after?

659
01:27:28,339 --> 01:27:33,242
Even that castle you conquered doesn't
belong to Kayıs, it belongs to me.

660
01:27:33,242 --> 01:27:37,362
And as a result, Kayıs' land
is my property.

661
01:27:38,461 --> 01:27:44,111
If you attack again, we'll fall out.

662
01:27:44,123 --> 01:27:46,393
We won't fall out.

663
01:27:47,090 --> 01:27:49,670
We should be clear to each other.

664
01:27:49,762 --> 01:27:53,132
Let's talk about it.

665
01:27:54,240 --> 01:27:57,390
I think we shouldn't threaten each other.

666
01:28:03,246 --> 01:28:04,916
We should do business.

667
01:28:05,806 --> 01:28:08,256
We should make each other rich.

668
01:28:09,745 --> 01:28:13,845
Am I not right?
We should think about our future.

669
01:28:15,970 --> 01:28:17,820
For instance...

670
01:28:18,040 --> 01:28:23,330
We can talk about Cobanogullari and
Rome's future.

671
01:28:24,058 --> 01:28:28,458
If Rome's future is conquering Karacahisar
and Sogut...

672
01:28:28,559 --> 01:28:32,873
that means you have not a future.

673
01:28:32,873 --> 01:28:39,093
Yavlak, if we go on threatening each
other like that...

674
01:28:39,543 --> 01:28:43,113
no one can have a future in this land.

675
01:28:45,518 --> 01:28:50,798
That evil Geyhatu leads both of us
by the nose.

676
01:28:52,223 --> 01:28:53,763
Right?

677
01:28:57,824 --> 01:29:00,104
Let me give you a secret.

678
01:29:00,534 --> 01:29:03,194
I actually like Turks.

679
01:29:06,829 --> 01:29:11,589
But those Kayıs...
How can I put this?

680
01:29:12,432 --> 01:29:14,692
They annoy me.

681
01:29:17,260 --> 01:29:21,880
I don't need your compassion, I
need your loyalty.

682
01:29:25,020 --> 01:29:27,430
I am going to go back to Kastamonu.

683
01:29:27,765 --> 01:29:30,445
Don't go behind my back.

684
01:29:30,951 --> 01:29:32,151
I promise.

685
01:29:33,311 --> 01:29:35,971
I won't backdoor you.

686
01:29:36,314 --> 01:29:38,974
We only will talk face to face.

687
01:29:47,862 --> 01:29:50,002
We'll see.

688
01:29:58,655 --> 01:30:01,195
So you like Turks, Nicola?

689
01:30:01,741 --> 01:30:03,111
Yes.

690
01:30:04,873 --> 01:30:06,823
When they are dead.

691
01:30:08,549 --> 01:30:12,559
I hope you didn't bring me here
just for this, Nicola.

692
01:30:13,763 --> 01:30:18,303
No, I got you out of prison so you
can learn fighting.

693
01:30:21,980 --> 01:30:25,720
There is no one who can beat me in
a duel in this land, Nicola.

694
01:30:26,443 --> 01:30:28,263
Vladius.

695
01:30:28,476 --> 01:30:32,566
Mother nature put the only thing
that defeat physical strength...

696
01:30:33,797 --> 01:30:35,087
here.

697
01:30:37,428 --> 01:30:42,658
The only thing that seperates us
from both Kayıs and Mongols is this.

698
01:30:43,769 --> 01:30:46,029
We just need to use it.

699
01:31:09,628 --> 01:31:11,558
Stop!

700
01:31:12,271 --> 01:31:15,971
Do not eat!

701
01:31:16,622 --> 01:31:20,182
This traitor poisoned the food.

702
01:31:20,363 --> 01:31:21,553
Eat.

703
01:31:22,127 --> 01:31:24,047
- You dog!
- Traitor!

704
01:31:24,047 --> 01:31:25,832
She killed my mother.

705
01:31:30,391 --> 01:31:32,791
Stop now! Stop!

706
01:31:41,670 --> 01:31:45,870
I will kill if you threaten me with
my life!

707
01:31:48,139 --> 01:31:52,039
Hazal Hatun, stop.
Calm down!

708
01:31:53,457 --> 01:31:54,977
Hazal Hatun!

709
01:31:55,586 --> 01:31:58,846
Calm down, Hazal Hatun!

710
01:31:59,310 --> 01:32:01,110
Calm down.

711
01:32:01,351 --> 01:32:03,311
Calm down.

712
01:32:10,245 --> 01:32:11,665
Calm down.

713
01:32:12,461 --> 01:32:14,531
Have a seat.

714
01:32:29,490 --> 01:32:31,000
Drink this.

715
01:32:34,517 --> 01:32:36,517
Hazal Hatun.

716
01:32:37,439 --> 01:32:39,429
Calm down.

717
01:32:43,584 --> 01:32:45,594
Calm down.

718
01:32:50,828 --> 01:32:55,558
She'll try again. We can't wait.
We need to do something.

719
01:32:55,639 --> 01:32:59,079
What needs to be done is clear!

720
01:32:59,096 --> 01:33:05,066
You saw who opposes your husband Savcı
and backs Osman up.

721
01:33:06,776 --> 01:33:09,416
I know, Hazal Hatun.

722
01:33:11,585 --> 01:33:14,625
I want you to cooperate with you and
defeat them.

723
01:33:19,741 --> 01:33:23,441
You were good with Bala.

724
01:33:23,718 --> 01:33:25,478
What is it?

725
01:33:25,975 --> 01:33:28,085
What happened?

726
01:33:28,561 --> 01:33:34,311
It wouldn't work. While our Beys are in
this situation, we Hatuns can't be friends.

727
01:33:39,856 --> 01:33:41,706
That's what I am talking about.

728
01:33:47,039 --> 01:33:52,329
She wasn't the only
fish in the sea, my Lena.

729
01:34:38,396 --> 01:34:40,886
Do you have to be that much private?

730
01:34:41,408 --> 01:34:46,228
Ertugrul Ghazi's son Savcı Bey.
First time has to be like this.

731
01:34:46,478 --> 01:34:50,659
We can't untie your eyes before you
untie your heart to us.

732
01:34:50,659 --> 01:34:55,339
I am with anyone who wants Kayı Tribe's
salute.

733
01:34:55,388 --> 01:34:58,288
Eyvallah, eyvallah. (thanks)

734
01:35:12,233 --> 01:35:14,333
“God Almighty speaks the truth.”

735
01:35:16,907 --> 01:35:23,447
Glorified is your Lord the Lord of Honour
and Power above what they claim!
[Saffah 37:180]

736
01:35:33,175 --> 01:35:36,285
May Allah please you, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

737
01:35:37,090 --> 01:35:38,700
Bey.

738
01:35:44,860 --> 01:35:46,990
Thank Allah, my Bey.

739
01:35:47,198 --> 01:35:48,638
Thank so much.

740
01:35:50,137 --> 01:35:52,437
What is new?

741
01:35:52,546 --> 01:35:57,756
Geyhatu arrived at the gates of our tribe
with his army, my Bey.

742
01:35:58,490 --> 01:36:03,600
He asked for Mongke with his commanders.

743
01:36:04,613 --> 01:36:08,923
Don't worry, my Bey.

744
01:36:09,036 --> 01:36:12,166
We didn't let them damage our tribe.

745
01:36:15,327 --> 01:36:19,417
What... what about my sons?

746
01:36:19,791 --> 01:36:22,141
Osman has shown up, my Bey.

747
01:36:22,573 --> 01:36:26,103
And Savcı brought Mongke.

748
01:36:27,098 --> 01:36:32,917
Osman disobeyed you, but, my Bey...

749
01:36:32,917 --> 01:36:37,137
He ruined Mongke's game and
saved his brother.

750
01:36:37,525 --> 01:36:41,955
He saved us from Geyhatu trouble.

751
01:36:49,293 --> 01:36:51,443
My Dark Osman.

752
01:37:00,986 --> 01:37:03,476
I need to decide...

753
01:37:06,192 --> 01:37:11,912
as soon as... possible...

754
01:37:21,803 --> 01:37:23,933
Long live my Bey.

755
01:37:32,881 --> 01:37:36,151
What is your aim, Savcı Bey?

756
01:37:36,603 --> 01:37:41,212
What do you want for Kayıs?

757
01:37:41,212 --> 01:37:43,942
When the night covers the sky...

758
01:37:44,037 --> 01:37:48,067
we shouldn't campaign.

759
01:37:48,344 --> 01:37:54,164
We should wait for the sun.
Let's see who is on our side!

760
01:37:54,865 --> 01:38:00,575
I want to make sure that I aim
the real enemy.

761
01:38:02,134 --> 01:38:05,294
We are few in number.
We should grow.

762
01:38:05,509 --> 01:38:09,249
We have lots of enemiies.
I want to have less enemies.

763
01:38:10,429 --> 01:38:16,389
I don't want my father Ertuğrul Ghazi's
relics to be wasted due to Mongols and Greeks.

764
01:38:17,557 --> 01:38:23,487
So that we can have only one enemy.

765
01:38:24,256 --> 01:38:28,726
And that brings us a successful campaign.

766
01:38:30,521 --> 01:38:32,561
That's what I think.

767
01:38:32,648 --> 01:38:34,908
Very well, Savcı Bey.

768
01:38:43,938 --> 01:38:49,468
You have the soul of a fighter, Lena.
You aimed fast, decided fast.

769
01:38:50,332 --> 01:38:51,882
I was lucky.

770
01:38:51,882 --> 01:38:55,122
It's not about luck, it's about practice.

771
01:38:55,585 --> 01:38:58,345
You know how to fight.

772
01:39:17,938 --> 01:39:20,938
- Welcome, my Bey.
- Thank you.

773
01:39:46,611 --> 01:39:49,817
I have chores to do.
I'll leave.

774
01:39:49,817 --> 01:39:52,307
Of course, sure.

775
01:40:14,323 --> 01:40:16,873
We will enter that castle today.

776
01:40:18,763 --> 01:40:22,543
- We are ready, my Bey.
- The command is yours, my Bey.

777
01:40:25,722 --> 01:40:27,912
Wait for my sign.

778
01:40:28,455 --> 01:40:31,535
- Eyvallah, my Bey.
- Eyvallah, my Bey. (okay)

779
01:41:17,497 --> 01:41:21,157
The only way to save your life is to
serve me.

780
01:41:23,261 --> 01:41:26,291
You know this, right, Cerkutay?

781
01:41:29,520 --> 01:41:32,120
It will cost dearly.

782
01:41:33,344 --> 01:41:35,784
Tell me your price.

783
01:41:36,346 --> 01:41:40,916
I want a slice of bloody meat.

784
01:41:42,508 --> 01:41:45,568
Prepare me a bed, so I can rest.

785
01:41:46,587 --> 01:41:50,017
And give me a beautiful woman.

786
01:41:56,358 --> 01:41:58,688
Is that all?

787
01:41:59,685 --> 01:42:01,885
Yes.

788
01:42:06,351 --> 01:42:11,481
But I want a delicious woman so that
I can do my duty well.

789
01:42:34,226 --> 01:42:37,486
This is the Mongol way, right?

790
01:42:39,538 --> 01:42:40,798
Nikola.

791
01:42:43,771 --> 01:42:47,551
The bait is taken.
Just as you estimated.

792
01:43:05,303 --> 01:43:08,403
This news saved your life, Cerkutay.

793
01:43:16,097 --> 01:43:19,537
But, you may not be this lucky next time.

794
01:43:24,017 --> 01:43:26,717
This is the third step, Flatyos.

795
01:44:16,127 --> 01:44:19,247
Osman will come to the castle with
Göktuğ and Boran.

796
01:44:23,104 --> 01:44:25,284
This is such good news.

797
01:44:26,670 --> 01:44:31,210
We need to tell Dündar Bey and Savcı Bey.

798
01:44:33,440 --> 01:44:34,720
Lena...

799
01:44:36,142 --> 01:44:41,362
Is it better for Osman to die in
that castle alone or...

800
01:44:41,502 --> 01:44:45,762
is it better if Savcı and
Dündar stops him?

801
01:44:53,257 --> 01:44:55,877
Come, Lena.
Come.

802
01:45:00,636 --> 01:45:03,356
Eat some walnut, it'll be
good for your brain.

803
01:45:10,163 --> 01:45:12,083
So, this is it.

804
01:46:29,999 --> 01:46:32,469
When I save my father...

805
01:46:33,349 --> 01:46:36,529
I'll shoot these arrows into
your mouth, Nikola.

806
01:46:48,434 --> 01:46:51,224
Targun made it, I guess.

807
01:46:58,954 --> 01:47:02,954
Osman... Nikola will be so
happy about this news.

808
01:47:22,116 --> 01:47:25,016
Karayel seems so hungry, my Osman Bey.

809
01:47:26,734 --> 01:47:28,934
It's Karayel, my valiant Ahmet.

810
01:47:30,223 --> 01:47:34,223
He has been in so
many wars and he's still fine.

811
01:47:37,700 --> 01:47:40,450
A horse is Turk's biggest comrade.

812
01:47:40,785 --> 01:47:43,595
A brother. A confidant.

813
01:47:44,450 --> 01:47:45,780
A wing, Ahmet.

814
01:47:50,301 --> 01:47:52,501
My dad once had a horse.

815
01:47:55,684 --> 01:47:58,174
He'd show me around with the horse.

816
01:48:02,212 --> 01:48:04,812
He loved his horse.

817
01:48:13,294 --> 01:48:15,134
He should come here.

818
01:48:17,534 --> 01:48:19,264
I missed him so much!

819
01:48:19,539 --> 01:48:20,539
So much!

820
01:48:24,834 --> 01:48:26,564
My Ahmet.

821
01:48:30,716 --> 01:48:32,926
I missed my father so much!

822
01:48:53,783 --> 01:48:55,303
My Ahmet.

823
01:48:56,161 --> 01:48:58,601
Don't cry, my valiant Ahmet.

824
01:48:59,490 --> 01:49:00,960
Don't cry.

825
01:49:01,991 --> 01:49:03,171
Now...

826
01:49:05,484 --> 01:49:08,654
Your father raises a
horse for you in heaven.

827
01:49:10,977 --> 01:49:12,417
Don't cry.

828
01:49:16,252 --> 01:49:18,922
I'll make you ride horses.

829
01:49:30,004 --> 01:49:31,054
My Bey.

830
01:49:33,305 --> 01:49:35,055
We're ready.

831
01:49:40,324 --> 01:49:41,444
Come on.

832
01:49:42,315 --> 01:49:43,715
Stop crying.

833
01:50:14,759 --> 01:50:18,759
You flame with vengeance for Osman and...

834
01:50:19,300 --> 01:50:21,330
I hope it doesn't burn you, Flatyos.

835
01:50:26,737 --> 01:50:27,987
Up!

836
01:50:28,738 --> 01:50:29,558
Up!

837
01:51:04,401 --> 01:51:07,931
We've started to reach
news from Kayı Tent.

838
01:51:44,958 --> 01:51:48,408
I told you Osman would come here.

839
01:51:49,188 --> 01:51:51,048
Is he coming?

840
01:51:52,217 --> 01:51:55,137
Targun succeeded in her first duty.

841
01:51:56,646 --> 01:51:59,196
Osman will come here.

842
01:52:01,165 --> 01:52:03,075
Alone.

843
01:52:20,477 --> 01:52:22,567
Nikola must have taken my message.

844
01:52:25,869 --> 01:52:27,739
He'll set my father free.

845
01:52:28,875 --> 01:52:31,625
- May it be easy.
- Thank you.

846
01:53:32,878 --> 01:53:34,588
Cerkutay...

847
01:53:37,108 --> 01:53:40,238
Cerkutay!
You're here!

848
01:53:40,806 --> 01:53:44,816
You're mad enough to confront me.

849
01:54:02,429 --> 01:54:04,469
I did what is asked for.

850
01:54:05,820 --> 01:54:10,080
When they understood what I
did, I became a man of Nikola.

851
01:54:11,785 --> 01:54:12,915
So?

852
01:54:14,209 --> 01:54:16,899
For you, Yavlak Arslan.

853
01:54:18,007 --> 01:54:19,687
Do you understand?

854
01:54:22,129 --> 01:54:23,569
Nice.

855
01:54:23,799 --> 01:54:25,109
Good.

856
01:54:25,584 --> 01:54:28,074
Your loyalty filled me with tears.

857
01:54:30,680 --> 01:54:32,700
You'll get what you deserve.

858
01:54:33,137 --> 01:54:35,247
I'm looking for it.

859
01:55:18,380 --> 01:55:22,080
Nikola, the lord of
Constantinople's Sultan...

860
01:55:23,161 --> 01:55:26,001
and Savcı Bey, Ertuğrul Ghazi's son...

861
01:55:26,191 --> 01:55:29,401
will discuss about war and..

862
01:55:32,386 --> 01:55:35,966
I, Yavlak Arslan...

863
01:55:36,152 --> 01:55:37,172
will---

864
01:55:38,663 --> 01:55:40,883
eff...
eff...--

865
01:55:42,813 --> 01:55:44,983
I'll make effort for it to happen.

866
01:55:45,362 --> 01:55:51,042
It's better if everyone gathers
and discusses.

867
01:55:51,360 --> 01:55:54,540
If the enemy wants peace...

868
01:55:54,592 --> 01:55:58,102
you'll want peace and trust Allah.

869
01:55:58,642 --> 01:56:00,982
I like to discuss.

870
01:56:01,168 --> 01:56:04,438
Of course we should discuss.

871
01:56:04,989 --> 01:56:08,989
Flatyos, when I waste Yavlak Arslan's
and...

872
01:56:08,989 --> 01:56:12,449
Savcı Bey's time talking about peace...

873
01:56:12,622 --> 01:56:15,542
you'll devastate Söğüt.

874
01:56:25,902 --> 01:56:28,592
I like this kind of peace, Nikola.

875
01:56:37,752 --> 01:56:41,802
Then, let's welcome Osman, Flatyos.

876
01:56:46,267 --> 01:56:49,107
Everyone in the castle is
waiting for Osman's arrival.

877
01:57:37,766 --> 01:57:40,206
I hope you come from this way, Osman.

878
01:58:48,448 --> 01:58:51,078
They knew we were coming.

879
01:58:55,632 --> 01:58:57,532
You know what to do.

880
02:00:13,071 --> 02:00:14,941
Where do you think he'll come, Nikola?

881
02:00:15,220 --> 02:00:18,770
It doesn't matter from where, if he comes.

882
02:00:20,078 --> 02:00:23,548
- He doesn't know we're waiting.
- He won't come if he knows

883
02:00:23,853 --> 02:00:25,003
Nice.

884
02:00:27,580 --> 02:00:29,230
It's Osman.

885
02:00:30,343 --> 02:00:31,293
He'll come.

886
02:00:31,613 --> 02:00:32,853
He will come.

887
02:00:33,092 --> 02:00:34,372
He will see.

888
02:00:34,925 --> 02:00:37,155
He will die, Flatyos.

889
02:00:37,532 --> 02:00:39,902
I want you to promise
me something, Nikola.

890
02:00:41,228 --> 02:00:43,338
I will kill Osman.

891
02:00:44,010 --> 02:00:46,820
- Now?
- Now. I'll kill him now.

892
02:00:46,900 --> 02:00:48,620
Why?

893
02:00:51,206 --> 02:00:53,316
Set the slaves free.

894
02:00:55,734 --> 02:00:59,734
Or, I'll cut this dog's throat.

895
02:00:59,791 --> 02:01:02,361
Don't let me go
if you don't kill me, Osman.

896
02:01:05,629 --> 02:01:09,059
- Let him go.
- I'll send him when I'm done with him.

897
02:01:20,623 --> 02:01:24,233
If a good hunter has a spear like this...

898
02:01:28,238 --> 02:01:30,268
he can hunt a lion.

899
02:01:30,520 --> 02:01:36,210
Because the lion can't pass the spear
and reach the hunter, Nikola.

900
02:01:37,089 --> 02:01:38,499
But...

901
02:01:39,383 --> 02:01:41,063
if the hunter realizes it and...

902
02:01:42,716 --> 02:01:45,496
tries to play a game with the lion...

903
02:01:50,628 --> 02:01:52,418
the lion will...

904
02:01:54,119 --> 02:01:56,499
use its paws, Nikola.

905
02:01:58,620 --> 02:02:00,990
Lion, huh? Lion.

906
02:02:02,543 --> 02:02:04,003
Flatyos.

907
02:02:04,229 --> 02:02:07,309
You sounded like you went through it.

908
02:02:22,869 --> 02:02:26,819
Hunter of lions, huh?
I didn't know that.

909
02:02:28,031 --> 02:02:29,031
Good.

910
02:02:29,275 --> 02:02:30,385
Good.

911
02:02:30,750 --> 02:02:32,790
Good.
Good.

912
02:02:32,950 --> 02:02:36,950
Let's kill him when he comes, Nikola.
- We'll do it slowly, Flatyos.

913
02:02:37,425 --> 02:02:40,245
Slowly.

914
02:06:52,807 --> 02:06:55,027
What are you waiting for? Take him!

915
02:07:56,751 --> 02:08:08,641
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com